          "Because MaxSim selects `max(score)` per query token independently rather than averaging across all document tokens, verbose reference manuals containing additional unrelated subsections are never penalized for extra length—explaining ColBERT's strong cross-domain generalization over length-sensitive BM25 or averaged dense pooling.",
