          "Maximal Marginal Relevance (MMR) solves the redundancy problem by greedily selecting candidates that maximize marginal novelty.",
          "The MMR formula evaluates: lambda * Sim(d, query) - (1 - lambda) * max_{s in Selected} Sim(d, s).",
          "The parameter lambda controls the trade-off: lambda=1.0 performs pure relevance search, while lambda=0.0 maximizes diversity.",
